          "text": "About this pattern"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A classic old-style telephone made from an oval base body and a capsule handset. A dial is embroidered on the front face of the base, and a curly yarn cord connects the handset to the body. Use a "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "glossaryTooltip",
              "attrs": {
                "termSlug": "colour-change"
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "colour change"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to add a contrast dial ring."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Telephone base"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Rounds: 18. Begin with a "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "glossaryTooltip",
              "attrs": {
                "termSlug": "magic-ring"
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "magic ring"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "glossaryTooltip",
              "attrs": {
                "termSlug": "amigurumi-increase"
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "increase"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to the widest point. Work the body straight, then "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "glossaryTooltip",
              "attrs": {
                "termSlug": "amigurumi-decrease"
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "decrease"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to close. Stuff firmly. A cradle for the handset can be shaped by gently flattening the top of the oval before closing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Round 1: Chain 14. Working along chain: 2 sc in 2nd ch from hook, sc in next 11 ch, 3 sc in last ch, rotate. Along opposite side: sc in next 11 ch, 2 sc in last ch (30 st)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Round 2: Increase 6 stitches evenly around (36 st)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
